  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Fostering the Strengthening of UPCEFE&apos;s Capacities for the Design, Formulation, and Execution of Provincial and/or Municipal Programs with External Financing for the Province of Rio Negro.</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project aims to contribute to the strengthening the Provincial Unit for Coordination and Execution of External Financing&apos;s (UPCEFE) capacities in order to increase the number and quality of provincial and/or municipal project proposals and documents that are presented to multilateral credit institutions, in line with the provincial public investment policy and Provincial Law. The strengthening of institutional capacities and government officials allows for the improvement of knowledge, skills, and actions of public organizations. The proposed modalities for strengthening UPCEFE&apos;s capacities are broad and include personnel training, mentoring, organizational development, support for the creation of provincial work networks, sectoral prioritization according to provincial needs, establishment of cooperation agreements, and the development of a results-based budget for UPCEFE that is not only structured by programs but also allows for the measurement of programmatic goals and objectives. Implementing these actions will improve UPCEFE&apos;s access to external financing to design and implement public policies that benefit all inhabitants of the province, including foreign and internal migrants, while simultaneously reversing recent patterns of emigration. Under this project, the IOM Country Office in Argentina will provide technical and administrative assistance to UPCEFE, which is responsible for the administration of project funds.</narrative>
  </description>
